A||||5||fropuff||Gauge wiring...||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||07-20-2001||12:53 AM||||Hey guys.  I'm looking to do some new gauge faces, but they require the gauge lights to be on when the ignition is on.  I'm wondering how I make the gauge lights operate simultaneously with the ignition.  I know I'll have to splice wires into other wires, but I'm not sure where to start.  If anyone knows, that'd be great.  Mentioning wire colors is also very helpful.  I'm a visual person.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks a lot!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-20-2001||01:22 AM||||I don't know what wires they would be, but i say best bet is to use a volt meter, and see what wires are hot when you turn the key on. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-20-2001||01:27 AM||||Pink wires are usually hot in run/start.<BR>Red wires are non-fused hot.<BR>Orange wires are fused hot.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||07-20-2001||09:32 AM||||Okay, thanks!  Now, which color wires should I splice into the ignition wiring?  For the gauges.  Should I turn the parking lamps on and do a volt meter check for the wires going to the gauges?  Thanks a lot!<P>------------------<BR>If it ain't broke, might as well slap on some nitrous!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||07-20-2001||11:07 AM||||wouldn't it be better to have them work off the dimmer with the rest of the gauges? thats what i did with my aftermarket ones.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||07-20-2001||11:15 AM||||I believe that the wires for all the lighting that is controlled by the interior lighting dimmer control (guages, radio, heater control, etc.) are brown in color.  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
